```

When middleware has already put a cookie on `c.res` and a handler returns a new `Response` that has its own `Set-Cookie` header, the setter deletes the new Response's cookies and only keeps the old ones. BOTH must survive after the fix.

Important runtime detail: in Node/undici, `Headers.entries()` yields ONE `'set-cookie'` entry PER cookie. So appending inside the loop would duplicate cookies. Capture `this.#res.headers.getSetCookie()` once and append the old cookies once after the loop, and skip `'set-cookie'` entirely in the loop (leave `_res`'s existing cookies untouched). Preserve the existing behavior for all other headers, including skipping `content-type`.

Suggested shape (adapt as you see fit, but keep it minimal and clear):

```ts
